{
  "abstract": "Can a Transformer train without a backward pass—zero pullbacks, VJP helpers, or same-step relays inside `with torch.no_grad():`—while beating matched-subset node perturbation? We study 3-stage delayed Weight Maximization (WM) across 212 backward-free arms (`exp26`–`exp74`, plus 3 compositional, 7 pullback, and 60 BP/surrogate arms; $282$ arms $=845$ runs) on `d6` ($L=6,D\\in\\{256..768\\}$, $360$–$1,004$st) and `50.3M` ($L=8,D=512,T=2,048$, $100$st). We prove stream-partitioned WM and its $\\operatorname{diag}(1-x_i^2/D)$ `RMSNorm` mean (Prop. 1), commute $W_v$ with attention ($+0.9069$ cos, Prop. 2), route `wte` via a diagonal skip (Prop. 3), bound `RMSNorm` residual by $\\kappa_4(x)/D$ (Prop. 4), prove tangent-projection variance drop (Prop. 5), derive the Wiener-MMSE key filter $W_{\\tau,s}^{\\text{MMSE}}(M)$ ($3.22\\times$ cos, Prop. 6), apply Zhang et al.'s [12] groupwise Stiefel polar factor $\\operatorname{St}(g d_h,D)^{H/g}$ via Exact-SVD controls (Prop. 7, `exp66`–`exp71`), and prove `Exact-SVD Taper` $s_r(\\gamma)=((1-\\gamma)+\\gamma\\hat{\\sigma}_r)/c(\\gamma)$ with threshold $\\hat{\\sigma}^*(\\gamma)$ alongside `PrePolar-Blend` ($\\gamma_{QK}=0.20$, Prop. 8, `exp72`–`exp74`). Triton cuts `d6` WM time $38.4\\times$. Across $D\\in\\{256..768\\}$ ($360$st), Per-Head Stiefel + MMSE+$H_4$ $M=4$ hits **`2.0726, 2.0443 [2.0382 Blend / 2.0377 SVD-Taper], 2.0317, 2.0274` DEV BPB—beating 4-mat BP (`2.0789..2.0433`) and recovering $99.0\\%,141.2\\%,106.8\\%,101.4\\%$ of shared-LR 6-mat BP (`2.0532->2.0316`), $46.8\\%$ of Per-Head BP (`1.9899`), and $59.3\\%$ of Sub-Block BP (`2.0052`)**. At $720$st ($D=384$), 6-mat WM hits **`1.9476\\pm0.0008` (`23.78s`, Blend) / `1.9465\\pm0.0007` (`209.56` PPL, SVD-Taper)—recovering $98.8\\%/100.9\\%$ of shared-LR BP (`1.9423->1.8904`) and $56.0\\%/57.2\\%$ of Per-Head BP (`1.8518`)**; $840$st $M=2$ hits **`1.9420` (`20.03s`)**. On `50.3M`, Triton speeds up `fwd+rule` $6.33\\times$, hitting **`1.8592` ($M=2$) and `1.8554` (`184.97` PPL, $M=4$)** vs. BP $1.6989$.",
  "author": "cartan_geodesic",
  "change_summary": "1. Substantive Algorithmic & Theoretical Extension — Un-Equilibrated Energy-Matched Linear Spectral Tapering ('Exact-SVD Taper', Proposition 8, exp73) vs. Equilibrated 'PrePolar-Blend' (exp72, exp74) on Noisy Per-Head (W_Q, W_K) Updates: On ClimbMix d6 Step-120 checkpoints (exp72 Part 1), M in {2, 4} Rademacher/Hadamard probes populate all d_h channels of each head block (sigma_min/sigma_max = 0.0253 on W_Q and 0.0067 on W_K vs. 0.0681 on W_V, noting that small observed singular values alone do not prove a mode is pure perturbation noise). We prove (Proposition 8) that for un-equilibrated Exact-SVD Taper (exact_svd_taper_batched in run_exp73), blending (1-gamma)*U_exact(G_h) + gamma*sqrt(d_h)*G_h/||G_h||_F and re-normalizing by 1/c(gamma) with c(gamma) = sqrt((1-gamma)^2 + 2*gamma*(1-gamma)*sigma_bar + gamma^2) <= 1 preserves exact singular vectors and exact update energy ||U_gamma||_F^2 = d_h while mapping singular values to s_r(gamma) = ((1-gamma) + gamma*sigma_hat_r)/c(gamma), strictly attenuating modes below the exact threshold sigma_hat_r < sigma_star(gamma) := (c(gamma) - (1-gamma))/gamma <= 1 and boosting modes above sigma_star(gamma) (verified in Check 4E on the 3-mode counterexample (sqrt(2.18), 0.9, 0.1) at gamma=0.2 where sigma_star(0.2)=0.858390 < 0.9 < 1 => s_2(0.2)=1.008565 > 1, and on diag(4,2,0,0) vs. diag(4,2,1,1)). We explicitly distinguish Exact-SVD Taper from our fast polynomial heuristic PrePolar-Blend (prepolar_blend_batched in run_exp72, run_exp64, run_exp65), whose 2-pass row/column L2 equilibration alters singular vectors/values before blending (e.g., mapping diag(4,2,1,1) -> I_4). 2. ClimbMix d6 360/720/840-Step Milestones, Exact-SVD Taper Deconfounding, MLP Row-Grouping Controls, and Descriptive 720-Step BP Controls (exp72 Arms 1-4, exp73 Arms 1-5): On d6 (3 seeds), PrePolar-Blend (gamma_QK=0.20) improves 360-step Fixed-QK+V from 2.0443 -> 2.0382 +- 0.0003 DEV BPB (2.0009 VAL-B, 269.55 PPL, 11.86s) and 720-step from 1.9548 -> 1.9476 +- 0.0008 DEV BPB (1.9124 VAL-B, 210.21 PPL, 23.78s, recovering 98.8% of the shared-LR 4-to-6-matrix Global-BP gain 1.9423->1.8904). Un-equilibrated Exact-SVD Taper (gamma_QK=0.20, exp73 Arms 1-2) reaches 2.0377 +- 0.0003 at 360st and 1.9465 +- 0.0007 at 720st (1.9115 VAL-B, 209.56 PPL, -0.0059 and -0.0078 BPB over untapered Exact SVD 2.0436 / 1.9543, recovering 100.9% of shared-LR 6-mat BP and 57.2% of matched PrePolar-Blend Global-BP 1.9423->1.8518). As a descriptive 720-step reference (without claiming causal percentage attribution across distinct BP vs. WM trajectories), 720-step PrePolar-Blend Global-BP (1.8530->1.8518 +- 0.0006, exp73 Arm 4) and Sub-Block-Skip BP (1.8920->1.8904 +- 0.0009, exp73 Arm 5) shift by -0.0012 and -0.0016 BPB. At 840 steps (matched ~20.0s time), Upper-Half M=2 PrePolar-Blend hits 1.9420 +- 0.0004 DEV BPB (1.9073 VAL-B, 206.99 PPL, 20.03s; run_exp64 signature verified via static AST check in verify_paper5.py). Partitioning mlp.c_fc into k_mlp=4 row groups (exp72 Arms 3-4) yields 2.0444 (360st) and 1.9546 (720st). 3. Long-Context Native 50,332,176 Scale-Transfer (exp74 Arms 1-2): On 8-layer T=2,048 Native 50.3M (d_h=128), equilibrated PrePolar-Blend (gamma_QK=0.20) improves Upper-Half (4,5,6,7) M=2 by -0.0158 DEV BPB (1.8750 -> 1.8592 +- 0.0002 DEV, 1.8450 +- 0.0003 VAL-B, 186.99 PPL in 5.57s/step, beating unblended M=4 1.8702 at half the SDPA probes) and improves M=4 by -0.0148 DEV BPB (1.8702 -> 1.8554 +- 0.0008 DEV, 1.8410 +- 0.0008 VAL-B, 184.97 PPL in 6.32s/step).",
